{{Short description|Soup made with cream}}
A '''cream soup''' is a [[soup]] prepared using [[cream]], [[light cream]], [[Half_and_half#Dairy_product|half and half]], or [[milk]] as a key ingredient.<ref name="De Gouy 2018"/> Sometimes the dairy product is added at the end of the cooking process, such as after a cream soup has been [[purée]]d.<ref name="Lam 2011"/>

A cream soup will often have a [[soup base]], prepared with ingredients such as onion, celery, garlic powder, [[celery salt]], butter, bacon drippings, flour, salt, pepper, [[paprika]], milk, light cream, and [[chicken stock]] or [[vegetable stock]].<ref name="Child 2010"/> Various vegetables or meats are then added to the base. Sometimes, [[Leftovers|leftover]] vegetables and meats are used in cream soups.<ref name="Goudiss Goudiss 1918"/>
